SUMMARY:Deadline: Claude Corps Fellowship
DESCRIPTION:Claude Corps is a national fellowship program from Anthropic pl
 acing early-career fellows full-time at nonprofits across America for one 
 year\, with the goal of extending AI's benefits to communities and buildin
 g fellows' AI skills. Anthropic funds the program and provides Claude expe
 rtise\; CodePath (America's largest collegiate CS education provider) is t
 he fellows' official employer of record and leads programming\; Social Fin
 ance leads measurement and evaluation. AMOUNT: $85\,000 full-time salary p
 lus benefits\; expansive Claude token budget\; relocation support as neede
 d. FELLOW EXPERIENCE: intensive Claude training at the start\; five hours 
 of ongoing weekly training throughout\; support from a CodePath mentor\; A
 nthropic office hours for technical questions\; and professional guidance 
 from the host organization manager. SAMPLE HOST ORGANIZATIONS: Braven (Chi
 cago)\, Code the Dream (Durham NC)\, Heartland Forward (Bentonville AR)\, 
 Montgomery County Food Bank (Conroe TX)\, Reef Environmental Education Fou
 ndation (Key Largo FL)\, StriveTogether (Cincinnati)\, YMCA of Greater Cha
 rlotte\, and more than 400 nonprofits total. ELIGIBILITY: anyone over 18 w
 ith under two years of full-time work experience\, regardless of education
 al background\; must be authorized to work in the US\; must be comfortable
  working with Claude and willing to relocate if necessary. COHORTS: Cohort
  1 (100 fellows\, starts October 2026) -- applications close 17 July 2026\
 ; Cohort 2 (starts January 2027) and Cohort 3 (starts August 2027) -- roll
 ing applications. Apply at https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-corps.\n\
 nOrganisation: Anthropic (funded)\; CodePath (employer of record)\; Social
  Finance (evaluation)\nLocation: USA\; in-person at host nonprofit organiz
 ations across America (placement location varies\; relocation support avai
 lable).\nAward: $85\,000 full-time annual salary plus benefits\, expansive
  Claude token budget\, and relocation support as needed. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: 12 months.\n\nMore: https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-co
 rps?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-corps?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA\; in-person at host nonprofit organizations across America (pl
 acement location varies\; relocation support available).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hibrides-biennial-artistic-research-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203816Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Híbrides: Small Embodied Data - Call for Contributions (
 2nd Edition)
DESCRIPTION:Híbrides is a biennial of artistic research co-organised by th
 e Axolot.cat collective and the DARTS (Design\, Art\, Technology and Socie
 ty) research group at the UOC in Barcelona. The second edition\, "Small Em
 bodied Data\," centres on the concept of classification -- approached thro
 ugh machine learning\, data science\, algorithmic systems\, and questions 
 of who designs classifiers\, under what ethical codes\, and to what end. T
 he biennial brings classification into dialogue with its previous themes o
 f Small Data (community-defined\, intentional data collection and analysis
 ) and Embodiment (bodily experience as a foundation of situated\, sensory 
 knowledge). Both academic and non-academic contributions are welcome. FORM
 ATS ACCEPTED: Oral Presentations (20 minutes\; artistic practice\, artisti
 c research\, or academic research projects\; may be video-recorded for a p
 ublic archive and developed into short papers)\; Performances (20-30 minut
 es\; must engage with the physical body\, stage\, and technology\; complet
 e works\, including previously presented work\; takes place in a multipurp
 ose space with technical support). SUBMISSION REQUIREMENTS: online form wi
 th abstract (max 1\,000 characters)\, professional biography (max 1\,000 c
 haracters)\, and link to representative materials (3-5 images\; video and 
 technical rider required for performances). HONORARIA: oral presentations 
 €100\; performances €400\; invoice required in both cases. Participant
 s must follow the event's code of conduct. Event runs 26-28 November 2026 
 at UOC Poblenou campus and Convent de Sant Agustí\, Barcelona. Deadline: 
 7 September 2026. Submit at https://hibrides.axolot.cat/opencall.html.\n\n
 Organisation: Axolot.cat collective and DARTS research group\, Universitat
  Oberta de Catalunya (UOC)\nLocation: Barcelona\, Spain\; UOC Poblenou cam
 pus and Convent de Sant Agustí. In-person attendance required.\nAward: Or
 al presentations: €100 honorarium (invoice required). Performances: €4
 00 honorarium (invoice required). No submission fee.\nDuration: Festival r
 uns 26-28 November 2026.\n\nMore: https://hibrides.axolot.cat/opencall.htm
 l?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://hibrides.axolot.cat/opencall.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Barcelona\, Spain\; UOC Poblenou campus and Convent de Sant Agust
 í. In-person attendance required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:new-inc-year-13-mentor-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203816Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260708
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260709
SUMMARY:Deadline: NEW INC Year 13 Mentor Open Call
DESCRIPTION:NEW INC\, the New Museum's cultural incubator\, is seeking ment
 ors for Year 13 of its program supporting creative practitioners at the in
 tersection of art\, design\, and technology. This is a call for mentors (c
 reative and business leaders)\, not for program members. TWO MENTOR TYPES:
  Dedicated Mentors ($500 honorarium) are matched one-on-one with a member 
 and commit to ongoing support throughout the year\; Office Hours Mentors (
 $300 honorarium) offer one-on-one sessions to the broader community on an 
 as-needed basis. All mentors receive a one-year All Access Plus membership
  to the New Museum\, invitations to special events including the annual DE
 MO Festival\, and access to community-only workshops\, talks\, and social 
 events. YEAR 13 PROGRAM TRACKS mentors may support: Art & Code\; Creative 
 Science\; Extended Realities\; Launchpad\; Social Architecture. KEY DATES:
  Mentor Open Call closes 8 July 2026\; Mentor Open House (virtual info ses
 sion) 17 June 2026\, 12-1pm ET (register via the site)\; mandatory Dedicat
 ed Mentor matchmaking ranking session 11 September 2026\; mandatory Dedica
 ted Mentor matchmaking event 18 September 2026\; Dedicated Mentor matches 
 announced 2 October 2026. Most NEW INC activities take place Monday-Friday
 \, 10am-6pm ET. Apply at https://www.newmuseum.org/new-inc/open-call/.\n\n
 Organisation: NEW INC (New Museum Incubator)\nLocation: New York\, NY\, US
 A\; primarily in-person at 250 Hudson St\, lower Manhattan. Some hybrid pa
 rticipation possible.\nAward: Dedicated Mentors: $500 honorarium. Office H
 ours Mentors: $300 honorarium. All mentors also receive a one-year All Acc
 ess Plus membership to the New Museum. No application fee.\nDuration: Year
  13 program (September 2026 onward)\; average 4-8 hours of engagement per 
 week.\n\nMore: https://www.newmuseum.org/new-inc/open-call/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.newmuseum.org/new-inc/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York\, NY\, USA\; primarily in-person at 250 Hudson St\, lower
  Manhattan. Some hybrid participation possible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cht-emerging-voices-ai-society-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203816Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: Center for Humane Technology: Emerging Voices in AI and S
 ociety Fellowship (Inaugural Cohort)
DESCRIPTION:CHT's inaugural Emerging Voices in AI and Society Fellowship pl
 aces 3 fellows (one per focus area) in a 6-month\, part-time program to de
 velop rigorous public-impact research and writing on how AI is reshaping s
 ociety. Fellows choose from 5 focus areas: (1) AI and Cognition — what A
 I does to human judgment\, critical thinking\, and intellectual independen
 ce\; (2) AI and Relationships — AI's effects on intimacy\, companionship
 \, and social bonds\; (3) AI and Surveillance — how AI enables monitorin
 g\, tracking\, and control\; (4) AI and Spirituality — AI's intersection
  with meaning\, transcendence\, and religious practice\; (5) Inside the Ma
 chine: AI From a Technologist's Perspective. Up to 2 focus areas per appli
 cation. DELIVERABLES: one flagship research piece\, report\, or long-form 
 essay for public impact\; 1-3 op-eds (placed in target outlets or CHT Subs
 tack)\; one podcast appearance (Your Undivided Attention or equivalent)\; 
 cohort meetings and bi-weekly check-ins. SUPPORT: bi-weekly guidance from 
 Senior Director of Strategy and Impact\; editorial\, communications and gr
 aphic design support\; media training and PR placement support\; CHT email
  address and Slack access\; listing on CHT's public fellows page. WHO SHOU
 LD APPLY: mid-career researchers (psychology\, sociology\, philosophy\, co
 gnitive science\, communications\, STS)\, policy analysts\, journalists co
 vering tech and society\, civil society advocates\, or technologists with 
 insider perspective. Strong preference for those with a public writing tra
 ck record (op-eds\, Substack\, peer-reviewed work) and some public presenc
 e. HOW TO APPLY: 1-2 page research proposal per topic (up to 2)\, CV/resum
 e (2 pages max)\, 2-minute video explaining fit\, writing sample. Deadline
 : Sunday 12 July 2026\, 11:59pm EST.\n\nOrganisation: Center for Humane Te
 chnology (CHT)\nLocation: Remote\, 10 hours/week overlapping with EST requ
 ired.\nAward: $30\,000 fixed stipend paid in three milestone-based tranche
 s. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 months: September 14\, 2026 through Ma
 rch 18\, 2027. 15 hours per week.\n\nMore: https://www.humanetech.com/fell
 owship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.humanetech.com/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, 10 hours/week overlapping with EST required.
END:VEVENT
