UID:fondsbjp-dossiersubsidie-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203816Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds BJP: Dossiersubsidie for Freelance Regional and Loc
 al Journalists (autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Dossiersubsidie is the Fonds BJP scheme for freelance regio
 nal and local journalists in the Netherlands who want to follow one subjec
 t properly rather than chase daily news\, funding up to EUR 19\,200 for si
 x months of sustained reporting on a single dossier. It is aimed at the ga
 p left by shrinking regional newsrooms\, where structural coverage of loca
 l government\, housing\, care or industry rarely gets paid time. ELIGIBILI
 TY: freelance journalists working in Dutch regional and local media only (
 staff journalists and national-only reporters are directed to the fund's o
 ther schemes). The fund also runs a year-round Vooronderzoekssubsidie of u
 p to EUR 8\,800 for preliminary research and a year-round Uitvoeringssubsi
 die of up to EUR 38\,600 for carrying out projects\, both open to all jour
 nalists. APPLICATION WINDOW: 17 August to 14 September 2026\, via the Fond
 s BJP subsidy portal. Online office hours on 8 September 2026\; questions 
 on 020 63 86 295.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Bijzondere Journalistieke Project
 en (Fonds BJP)\nLocation: Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working 
 on Dutch regional and local reporting\nAward: Up to EUR 19\,200 for six mo
 nths of work on a single reporting dossier. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Six months of dedicated reporting on one subject area\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working on Dutch regional 
 and local reporting
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:programme-pause-2026-autumn@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203816Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Programme PAUSE: Emergency Hosting for Scientists and Art
 ists in Exile (autumn 2026 call)
DESCRIPTION:PAUSE is the French national programme for the emergency hostin
 g of scientists and artists in exile\, created in 2017 and run from the Co
 llege de France. It co-funds a stay at a French higher education or resear
 ch establishment or at a cultural institution so that a researcher\, docto
 ral candidate or artist at risk can keep working\, and it also supports th
 eir family. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be able to prove status as a doct
 oral student (with a thesis in progress interrupted by the emergency)\, re
 searcher\, teacher-researcher or artist-teacher in their country of origin
 \; must be in a crisis situation because of the security situation in that
  country or because of persecution or fear of persecution on grounds of et
 hnicity\, religion\, political convictions\, opinions or sexual orientatio
 n\, or the content of their research or teaching\; and must be forced into
  exile or have been in France for less than three years. HOST REQUIREMENT:
  a French host institution is mandatory and submits the application\; elig
 ible hosts are institutions under the French higher education and research
  ministry\, EESPIG private institutions\, and structures supported by the 
 Ministry of Culture. PAUSE publishes a list of at-risk candidates looking 
 for a host\, which institutions can use to find a match. The call opens at
  the end of August 2026 with a deadline of 24 September 2026.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Programme PAUSE\, hosted by the College de France\, with the French M
 inistries of Higher Education and Research and of Culture\nLocation: Franc
 e (hosting at a French higher education\, research or cultural institution
 )\nAward: PAUSE co-funds the hosting project (salary and support costs) to
 gether with the host institution\; amounts depend on the project and insti
 tution. No application fee.\nDuration: Hosting periods are typically 12 mo
 nths\, renewable subject to review\n\nMore: https://www.programmepause.fr/
 en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.programmepause.fr/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France (hosting at a French higher education\, research or cultura
 l institution)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
